React UI performs well if carefully tuned (virtualization, memoization, event delegation), but a Rust backend is justified for native filesystem access, indexing, binary parsing, and sandboxed plugin execution via Tauri. Performance strategies include minimizing React reconciliation using signals or fine-grained state libraries, offloading heavy tasks to Rust workers, and avoiding unnecessary hydration in desktop apps. Measuring key metrics like startup time, input latency, and indexing speed is essential.
