  - `crates/fs/` — filesystem ops, watch, debounced writes
  - `crates/indexer/` — inverted index, graph builder
  - `crates/plugin_host/` — plugin sandbox, capability gates
  - `crates/api/` — Tauri commands, DTOs (mirrored TS types via `ts-rs` if desired)
- `docs/` — architecture, decisions, perf budgets (already added)
- `tests/` — integration/contract tests (JS/TS and Rust)

**Inside `src/app-shell/`**
- `layout/` — pane tree model, split/tab components
- `navigation/` — command palette, quick switcher
- `chrome/` — sidebars, status bar, top bar
- `providers/` — context providers (theme, hotkeys, error boundary)

**State organization (`src/state/`)**
- `stores/`
  - `paneStore.ts` — pane tree, tabs, splits
  - `workspaceStore.ts` — vault selection, recents, session restore
  - `settingsStore.ts` — user prefs, feature flags
- `selectors/` — derive slices to prevent over-render
- `effects/` — orchestrate cross-store reactions (e.g., close tab -> flush dirty doc)
- Keep React Query (or equivalent) caches near their feature in `features/*/queries.ts`.

**Services**
- `services/fsClient.ts` — Tauri command wrappers (read/write/list/watch)
- `services/searchClient.ts` — RPC to Rust indexer/worker
- `services/pluginHost.ts` — message bridge to plugin worker/native host
- `services/metrics.ts` — perf logging hooks

**Workers**
- `workers/indexer/` — tokenizer + inverted index + link graph (JS) or bridge to Rust
- `workers/preview/` — markdown → HTML, math, code fences (off-main-thread)
- Use `comlink` or a thin RPC; keep payloads delta-based.

**Feature folders (`src/features/*`)**
- Each feature keeps `components/`, `queries/`, `state/`, `types/`, and optional `worker/` stubs.
- Examples: `features/file-explorer`, `features/search`, `features/backlinks`, `features/graph`, `features/settings`, `features/command-palette`.

**Rust side guidelines**
- `crates/fs/`: focused on fast directory scans, debounced writes, and file watching.
- `crates/indexer/`: incremental index; expose streaming results (chunked/binary) to the UI.
- `crates/plugin_host/`: capability-checked APIs for plugins; no direct fs/network without gating.
- Use a small `tauri::command` surface in `crates/api/` to keep the JS bindings stable.

**Why this works**
- Feature folders keep UI coherent and limit blast radius.
- Services/workers keep heavy work out of React and the main thread.
- Separate `packages/editor` and `packages/ui` lets you reuse primitives and keep the shell light.
- Rust crates mirror concerns (fs, indexer, plugin host) so you can evolve them independently.

